    "title": "March 20 Conference Explores Women's Lives During Long Island's Seven-Year British Occupation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chris Boyle ,\n21 hours ago During the American Revolution, Long Island remained under British occupation for more than seven years — longer than anywhere else in the country. On Friday, March 20, the Mastics-Moriches-Shirley Community Library will host a conference exploring how women across the island endured and navigated that extraordinary period in history. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
